      "start_byte": 1062557
    },
    {
      "end_byte_exclusive": 1064250,
      "occurrence_count_in_frozen_authority": 1,
      "old_bytes": 62,
      "old_sha256": "FF2D48E0F15A6B060EB42247A7ABA49E76FBF99FB1235104BB8F5FC2891E276F",
      "old_text": "structural results on Artinian rings implies parts (1) and (2)",
      "operation_index": 1,
      "producer_id": "ALGEBRA-275",
      "replacement_bytes": 60,
      "replacement_sha256": "212F489513644B799DDF0444D0C415E54BEEBB6BA75CF9D1032A63830C4F728F",
      "replacement_text": "structural results on Artinian rings imply parts (1) and (2)",
      "source_end_line": 29261,
      "source_start_line": 29261,
      "start_byte": 1064188
    },
    {
      "end_byte_exclusive": 1066471,
      "occurrence_count_in_frozen_authority": 1,
      "old_bytes": 65,
      "old_sha256": "F69FBD7DDEA24A88981D881C25A25D073A9043E080BAE24C87983C655FA7EAB4",
      "old_text": "Then there exists discrete valuation ring $A$ with fraction field",
      "operation_index": 1,
      "producer_id": "ALGEBRA-276",
      "replacement_bytes": 67,
      "replacement_sha256": "91B2E44903100B54C959B0544D6A145F9AFE0B15610DD1BA2FCC31845E56C62D",
      "replacement_text": "Then there exists a discrete valuation ring $A$ with fraction field",
      "source_end_line": 29316,
      "source_start_line": 29316,
      "start_byte": 1066406
    },
    {
      "end_byte_exclusive": 1067963,
      "occurrence_count_in_frozen_authority": 1,
      "old_bytes": 96,
      "old_sha256": "23AC8537A5D6290BC6A207C63AA4F70514083A27CB77192D3220D6FE4F01D677",
      "old_text": "\\item An element $x \\in R$ is called {\\it prime} if the ideal\ngenerated by $x$ is a prime ideal.",
      "operation_index": 1,
      "producer_id": "ALGEBRA-277",
      "replacement_bytes": 103,
      "replacement_sha256": "FE49A06A56E000C8E4260995A0CA52414D9CBD14E929F760B23BA128C787B945",
      "replacement_text": "\\item A nonzero element $x \\in R$ is called {\\it prime} if the ideal\ngenerated by $x$ is a prime ideal.",
      "source_end_line": 29364,
      "source_start_line": 29363,
      "start_byte": 1067867
    },
    {
      "end_byte_exclusive": 1068359,
      "occurrence_count_in_frozen_authority": 1,
      "old_bytes": 22,
      "old_sha256": "93D21328FEAE6705B266AB69699D91AB8BB86E127BB37DBA2D906E93DD58CA7A",
      "old_text": "for some $f, g \\in A$.",
      "operation_index": 1,
      "producer_id": "ALGEBRA-278",
      "replacement_bytes": 22,
      "replacement_sha256": "532B2AD8F9FBC604595CD2A2C4C468D431EA9A03CCD446C7967723C48B7D9781",
      "replacement_text": "for some $f, g \\in R$.",
      "source_end_line": 29377,
      "source_start_line": 29377,
      "start_byte": 1068337
    },
    {
      "end_byte_exclusive": 1068416,
      "occurrence_count_in_frozen_authority": 1,
      "old_bytes": 56,
      "old_sha256": "D3BC5C2BEA3CE33B7A353D5C82E20D24D5C6DA10282F8A0A86C5CD9924ED870C",
      "old_text": "Then $x = fg x$ and since $R$ is a domain $fg = 1$. Thus",
      "operation_index": 1,
      "producer_id": "ALGEBRA-279",
      "replacement_bytes": 126,
      "replacement_sha256": "C88E0D8244EE76B92E5556F2120F736ADEE2A3841FD1C7BE452B2915526B23E5",
      "replacement_text": "If $x = 0$, then also $y = 0$, and the conclusion is immediate.\nOtherwise, $x = fg x$ and since $R$ is a domain $fg = 1$. Thus",
      "source_end_line": 29378,
      "source_start_line": 29378,
      "start_byte": 1068360
    },
    {
      "end_byte_exclusive": 1070318,
      "occurrence_count_in_frozen_authority": 1,
      "old_bytes": 56,
      "old_sha256": "B79514F43935680CEC08A8792A2271950C3F1896127E08B09289E04EBB94DFA5",
      "old_text": "Say $ab \\in (x)$, i.e., $ab = cx$. Choose factorizations",
      "operation_index": 1,
      "producer_id": "ALGEBRA-281",
      "replacement_bytes": 184,
      "replacement_sha256": "996AE3783C801902BDDE828D9DF5FA63F52756E0E0F56B769ABCAA57D2C79E78",
      "replacement_text": "Say $ab \\in (x)$, i.e., $ab = cx$. If $a = 0$ or $b = 0$, the\nconclusion is immediate. Thus $a$, $b$, and $c$ are nonzero. Choose\nfactorizations (allowing the empty product for a unit)",
      "source_end_line": 29435,
      "source_start_line": 29435,
      "start_byte": 1070262
    },
    {
      "end_byte_exclusive": 1071262,
      "occurrence_count_in_frozen_authority": 1,
      "old_bytes": 156,
      "old_sha256": "B6AB00342A608842AD6557F5C5276E6BBB80AABEB555F2BA33B90C75DFE252A8",
      "old_text": "and $a_2 \\ldots a_n = ub_2\\ldots b_m$. By induction on $n + m$\nwe see that $n = m$ and $a_i$ associate to $b_{\\sigma(i)}$ for\n$i = 2, \\ldots, n$ as desired.",
      "operation_index": 1,
      "producer_id": "ALGEBRA-282",
      "replacement_bytes": 257,
      "replacement_sha256": "897AF75E30941CB5F5B8379FE3FB94FCB3219D5B58D7073BA9685AFA86BB6152",
      "replacement_text": "and $a_2 \\ldots a_m = ub_2\\ldots b_n$. If $m = 1$ or $n = 1$,\nthis equality forces $m = n = 1$. Otherwise, absorb $u$ into $b_2$\nand apply induction on $n + m$ to see that $n = m$ and $a_i$ is\nassociate to $b_{\\sigma(i)}$ for $i = 2, \\ldots, n$, as desired.",
      "source_end_line": 29455,
      "source_start_line": 29453,
      "start_byte": 1071106
    },
    {
      "end_byte_exclusive": 1075223,
      "occurrence_count_in_frozen_authority": 1,
      "old_bytes": 68,
      "old_sha256": "3D4FFC752C83642F65901DCE693DFBC00FF4043F758F0B2C176C5D74765A1854",
      "old_text": "of principal ideals in $R$. Write $a_1 = p_1^{e_1} \\ldots p_r^{e_r}$",
      "operation_index": 1,
      "producer_id": "ALGEBRA-283",
      "replacement_bytes": 215,
      "replacement_sha256": "192894F0D12D30C96AE81D5ECDCDB055132DA5BDA0D1335ED7F0150E859D8B6B",
      "replacement_text": "of principal ideals in $R$. If $a_n = 0$ for every $n$, there is\nnothing to prove. Otherwise, after dropping an initial segment and\nrenumbering, we may assume $a_1 \\not = 0$. Write\n$a_1 = p_1^{e_1} \\ldots p_r^{e_r}$",
      "source_end_line": 29550,
      "source_start_line": 29550,
      "start_byte": 1075155
    },
