      "old_sha256": "A3BF2581BE10EDA68491E833D30CBB64C760FC40D4CD0617CA3C32D2810D5332",
      "old_text": "of principal ideals in $R[x]$. Since",
      "operation_index": 1,
      "producer_id": "ALGEBRA-284",
      "replacement_bytes": 183,
      "replacement_sha256": "B3154D0C9A7610CEC8174988367F35F3BAC4737F7A4ABE3A4096428BC41B95FF",
      "replacement_text": "of principal ideals in $R[x]$. If $f_n = 0$ for every $n$, there is\nnothing to prove. Otherwise, after dropping an initial segment and\nrenumbering, we may assume $f_1 \\not = 0$. Since",
